WEBVTT

00:11:29.414 --> 00:11:30.810
What that means in practice

00:11:30.834 --> 00:11:34.376
is you don't need huge accomplishments
to feel good about your work.

00:11:34.400 --> 00:11:38.976
What matters most for building
efficacy is small wins.

00:11:39.000 --> 00:11:42.856
Often those small wins come from having
a positive impact on others.

00:11:42.880 --> 00:11:45.846
I found in my research
that when people feel ineffective,

00:11:45.870 --> 00:11:48.546
helping others buffers against burnout.

00:11:48.570 --> 00:11:50.026
It makes them feel competent,

00:11:50.050 --> 00:11:52.603
which leaves them energized
rather than exhausted.

00:11:54.040 --> 00:11:56.950
For Conrey, tutoring high-achieving
students on the weekends

00:11:56.974 --> 00:11:58.806
was full of small wins.

00:11:58.830 --> 00:12:00.666
She could see their progress quickly,